Taxonomy: US GAAP 2026
**/


rule-name-prefix DQC

/** V32 Release **/
/**

Overview: This rule checks if the BDC uses an extensible enumeration and uses the KVP for that extensible enumeration then the value should match.

The value of an extensible enumeration fact is a set of qnames. The KVP value for the related key must match the local name (member name) of one of those qnames.

**/

/** Each extensible enumeration element and the KVP key that reports the same attribute **/
constant $ENUM_KVP_KEYS = dict(list(InvestmentIssuerAffiliationExtensibleEnumeration, 'AFF'),
							list(InvestmentIssuerGeographicRegionExtensibleEnumeration, 'GEO'),
							list(InvestmentIndustrySectorExtensibleEnumeration, 'IND'),
							list(InvestmentIssuerNameExtensibleEnumeration, 'ISS'),
							list(InvestmentTypeExtensibleEnumeration, 'TYP'))

ASSERT US.0259.10984 SATISFIED

$rule_id = (rule-name().split('.'))[rule-name().split('.').length];

/** DQCRT RULE **/
if not $BDC_FLAG
	skip
else

$fact = {@concept in $ENUM_KVP_KEYS.keys @InvestmentIdentifierAxis = *}

$factKVP = $fact.dimension(InvestmentIdentifierAxis)

if not is_kvp_member($factKVP)
	skip
else
	$kvpKey = $ENUM_KVP_KEYS[$fact.concept.name];
	$kvpValue = get_dim_key_value($factKVP.string, $kvpKey);
	/** If the key is not in the KVP there is nothing to compare. Missing required keys are reported by DQC.US.0246. **/
	if $kvpValue == none
		skip
	else
		/** Filtering over the fact iterates the qnames in its value. $fact.local-name would return the local name of the concept, not the value. **/
		$enumValueNames = (filter $fact returns $item.local-name).to-set;
		$kvpValue not in $enumValueNames

message
"The fact with concept name {$fact.concept.name} and a value of {$fact} is an extensible enumeration and has no corresponding Key Value Pair (KVP) in the InvestmentIdentifierAxis.  The value of the extensible enumeration fact should be a value specified in the KVP.

The InvestmentIdentifierAxis member {$factKVP} reports the key {$kvpKey} with a value of {$kvpValue}.  This does not match the value of the extensible enumeration fact {$fact}.  Please ensure the extensible enumeration value and the KVP value for the key {$kvpKey} identify the same item.

Rule Element Id:{$rule_id}
Rule version: {$ruleVersion}"

severity error
rule-focus $fact
effectiveDate $effective_dates[$rule_id]
